      "content": "Revision: Call Function By Value"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The normal way of calling a function, where we pass the values of variables as arguments, is known as calling a function by value. For example,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "1#include <iostream>\n2using namespace std;\n3\n4void display_name(string name_arg) {\n5    cout << \"Name: \" << name_arg << endl;\n6}\n7\n8int main() {\n9\n10    string name = \"Sheev Palpatine\";\n11\n12    // call display_name() by value\n13    display_name(name);\n14\n15    return 0;\n16}\n17\n18// Output\n19// Name: Sheev Palpatine"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, only a copy of the value of the name variable is passed to the function. Thus, the function argument name_arg is independent of the name variable in the main() function."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "A copy of the variable value is passed to the function when calling by value in C++",
